    {
      "id": "thm-least-squares-fitted-vector-and-solution-set",
      "path": "items/thm-least-squares-fitted-vector-and-solution-set.md",
      "raw_sha256": "bee6f79cb28092122995b81eecd51ebd1c36810579af425709d80072547a5f65",
      "archive": "research/statistical-models-experiments-62-owner-regression-archive/bee6f79cb28092122995b81eecd51ebd1c36810579af425709d80072547a5f65.source",
      "native_held": false,
      "disposition": "unchanged-sound prerequisite/support context",
      "finding": "Actual generic finite-dimensional LS, real adjoint transpose, nearest projection and rank-nullity suppliers establish nonempty normal-equation solution affine kernel, unique fit/residual and dimension p-rank X."
    },
    {
      "id": "def-linear-estimability-in-fixed-design",
      "path": "items/def-linear-estimability-in-fixed-design.md",
      "raw_sha256": "89a038fa902c5f90c3a3b711a17d11f6b91cba298cc5d650782ec8854d195fed",
      "archive": "research/statistical-models-experiments-62-owner-regression-archive/89a038fa902c5f90c3a3b711a17d11f6b91cba298cc5d650782ec8854d195fed.source",
      "native_held": true,
      "disposition": "unchanged-sound; original unavailable-interface finding resolved",
      "finding": "Correctly restricts estimability to fixed linear measurable statistic a^T Y, unbiased for every beta in all of R^p. a may depend on design/contrast, not response/parameter. Measurability supplied by actual local lemma; integrability follows from coordinate integrability and finite linearity."
    },
    {
      "id": "thm-linear-estimability-iff-row-space",
      "path": "items/thm-linear-estimability-iff-row-space.md",
      "raw_sha256": "d7b62005e1f6c05d3bc67fb2a371a7a468c7f91d51785165cb797662785bd2bd",
      "archive": "research/statistical-models-experiments-62-owner-regression-archive/d7b62005e1f6c05d3bc67fb2a371a7a468c7f91d51785165cb797662785bd2bd.source",
      "native_held": true,
      "disposition": "unchanged-sound; original unavailable-interface finding resolved",
      "finding": "Expectation calculation gives (X^T a)^T beta. All-beta unbiasedness forces X^T a=c by coordinate basis tests, and the converse follows by substitution. Row(X) is explicitly defined as im(X^T). Rank-deficient and zero X cases preserved; no nonlinear-estimator impossibility claim."
    },
    {
      "id": "thm-ols-unbiasedness-and-covariance-full-rank",
      "path": "items/thm-ols-unbiasedness-and-covariance-full-rank.md",
      "raw_sha256": "ac355a728166b62acfac470155217053d7ce59a2c962882ab7be1f05100b415f",
      "archive": "research/statistical-models-experiments-62-owner-regression-archive/ac355a728166b62acfac470155217053d7ce59a2c962882ab7be1f05100b415f.source",
      "native_held": true,
      "disposition": "unchanged-sound; original unavailable-interface finding resolved",
      "finding": "Positive definiteness v^T X^T X v=||Xv||^2 for nonzero v under full rank proves invertibility using finite rank-nullity. Actual LS normal equations give unique coefficient estimate. Bounded linear coordinate maps are measurable; finite square-integrable error coordinates give finite moments. AX=I yields unbiasedness; actual covariance bilinearity gives sigma^2 AA^T=sigma^2(X^T X)^-1, with no Gaussianity."
    },
    {
      "id": "thm-gauss-markov-for-fixed-design-regression",
      "path": "items/thm-gauss-markov-for-fixed-design-regression.md",
      "raw_sha256": "d1c47fdba107c57c1b25d8f5268f8b9665a9d23d296fc0a49adbe9e136ef46be",
      "archive": "research/statistical-models-experiments-62-owner-regression-archive/d1c47fdba107c57c1b25d8f5268f8b9665a9d23d296fc0a49adbe9e136ef46be.source",
      "native_held": true,
      "disposition": "unchanged-sound; original unavailable-interface finding resolved",
      "finding": "Current statement defines vector covariance entrywise through local covariance convention, which is only defined for square-integrable variables. Therefore finite second moments in A1 follow from the covariance premise; first-moment model gives mean-zero errors. For each contrast, a0=X(X^T X)^-1 c; any unbiased fixed linear competitor a obeys X^T a=c. q=a-a0 has X^T q=0 and q^T a0=0. Variance difference sigma^2||q||^2 is nonnegative, with equality iff q=0. Preserves full-column-rank, positive sigma^2 and moment-only scope."
    },
    {
      "id": "ex-collinear-fixed-design-estimability",
      "path": "items/ex-collinear-fixed-design-estimability.md",
      "raw_sha256": "125e0c3f9ca1211372af87e45a7802bf61de5e8c1064dd0ccb55ee5fb698da36",
      "archive": "research/statistical-models-experiments-62-owner-regression-archive/125e0c3f9ca1211372af87e45a7802bf61de5e8c1064dd0ccb55ee5fb698da36.source",
      "native_held": true,
      "disposition": "unchanged-sound; original unavailable-interface finding resolved",
      "finding": "Displayed rank-one X yields residual objective 2(s-2)^2+2, full solution family (1,1)+t(1,-1), fit (2,2), residual (-1,1). Row space is span(1,1); sum contrast has a=(1/2,1/2), both individual coefficient contrasts lack equal coordinates. All numerical and estimability claims sound."
    },
    {
      "id": "cex-heteroskedasticity-invalidates-ols-blue",
      "path": "items/cex-heteroskedasticity-invalidates-ols-blue.md",
      "raw_sha256": "f89be4c71c133676d4d1ae72cf2dc455d3fe55baac5753c14c2be524a54e9e1d",
      "archive": "research/statistical-models-experiments-62-owner-regression-archive/f89be4c71c133676d4d1ae72cf2dc455d3fe55baac5753c14c2be524a54e9e1d.source",
      "native_held": true,
      "disposition": "unchanged-sound; original unavailable-interface finding resolved",
      "finding": "Uniform four-atom sign construction gives E U=E V=E UV=0 and unit sign variances. Error covariance diag(1,9) fails scalar-I premise; response law for every beta is its pushforward under Y=(beta+U,beta+3V), hence is a first-moment regression model on Borel R^2. OLS average variance is 5/2; competitor coefficients (9/10,1/10) sum to one and variance is 9/10. Counterexample derives OLS by direct elementary minimization formula and does not import the homoskedastic covariance theorem outside its domain."
    },
    {
